#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f120ae90-3df2-56d4-8a21-38c801f60d72" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a First-Order Inhomogeneous ODE With Polynomial Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3035f1a-da0f-5e21-ac30-8bdb476d3fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Ae^{-2x}+2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3035f1a-da0f-5e21-ac30-8bdb476d3fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Ae^{-2x}+2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238169} :answer-field/id #uuid "f49a36a3-cb09-5861-898a-864f8fc3875b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ff46deb-925a-5c83-8b7c-6a6d4330dad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-332270" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y = 4x + 2$.\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is $y_{c}(x) = Ae^{-2x}$, where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x) =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Try $y_p=ax+b$. Substitution into $y^{\\prime}+2y=4x+2$ gives $2ax+(a+2b)=4x+2$, so $a=2$ and $b=0$. Thus $y_p=2x$. Adding the supplied complementary solution gives $y(x)=Ae^{-2x}+2x$."}]}
